From: Codex <codex@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] uxtheme: read Windows Vista and 7 visual styles (format 4)

Purpose: let Windows 7's shell and the applications of its session draw
with Windows 7's aero.msstyles (Windows 7 Basic: the style without
desktop composition).
Windows 7 behavior: a format 4 theme (PACKTHEM_VERSION 4) has no ini text.
VMAP names its variants (resource, size and color names). CMAP lists the
class names ("TaskBar2::TaskBar"); a VARIANT resource holds the variant's
properties as records of property id, primitive type, class index, part,
state, a resource id and the size of the data that follows, padded to
eight bytes. With a resource id nothing follows: fonts and some
rectangles are strings of the theme's string table, in its MUI file
(ja-JP\aero.msstyles.mui: "Meiryo, 9, Quality:ClearType"), and image
files are IMAGE resources, PNG with alpha already multiplied into the
colors (no color of any of aero.msstyles' 600 images exceeds its alpha;
Windows 7 draws the AltTab class's translucent parts as that data
blended as is). Enumerations are numbers.
A class takes the properties it does not define from a base class: BCMAP
holds, after a count, the base of each class as an index counted from
"globals" in CMAP, or -1 (Tooltip has TooltipStyle as its base, which
defines TextColor; ItemsView::ListView has Explorer::ListView).
Wine before: themes of any format but 3 were rejected ("Version of theme
file is unsupported: 0x0004") and Windows 7 drew its classic look.
Change: a format 4 theme opens with the colors and sizes of VMAP and the
variant that matches. When it becomes active, each record becomes the text
a format 3 ini would give (enumerations by their names, a number when the
name map lacks the value) in the classes, parts and states of the
existing reader, with sysmetrics applied as SysMetrics; the strings come
from <dir>\<UI language>\<file>.mui, else en-US, else the theme. An
application's class takes what it lacks from the class of the same name,
then globals; a class with a base in BCMAP takes it from that base
instead (a base that would make a loop is ignored, and a class that only
has a base is created so it can be opened). Images load from the IMAGE resource through WIC as 32 bpp
DIB sections and go through the same alpha preparation as format 3 ones,
without the multiplication by alpha that they already have.
Evidence: Windows 7 SP1 explorer.exe draws the Basic taskbar, Start
button and dialog frames and buttons with aero.msstyles. XP's Luna and
classic scenes (13 scenes, nested session) are pixel-identical with and
without the patch. Without base classes, GetThemeColor(Tooltip, 1, 0,
TMT_TEXTCOLOR) failed and Windows 7's DirectUI stopped building its folder
windows at the scroll tip; with them it is 0x575757. DrawThemeBackground
of the AltTab class's five parts over magenta, and the Basic taskbar's
background, are pixel-identical to Windows 7 SP1's (a reference VM).
Scope: format 4 themes only; format 3 themes (XP, ReactOS) read as before.
